{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry your computer is acting up again. I can't see the earlier ticket from here, so I need a few details to work out what's going on: 1) What exactly is happening? For example: slow or freezing, crashing or blue screens, won't turn on, won't connect to Wi-Fi or the network, or an error message (a screenshot or the exact wording helps). 2) When did it start this time, and roughly how often does it happen? 3) Did it start after an update or after installing a new app? 4) When did you last fully restart the laptop (Start > Power > Restart, not just closing the lid)? Also, your laptop hasn't connected to our network in about 12 days. Could you turn it on, connect to the office network or VPN, and let me know if it won't connect? If it's running slow in the meantime, a full restart often helps. Thanks!",
  "internal_note": "The ticket is vague ('doing the thing again') and there is no prior ticket history I can see. User 7, Sofia Rossi (Marketing, not VIP). Account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked, VPN enabled. Device BL-LT-0107 (Win 11 Pro): OFFLINE, last check-in 2026-09-27, warning 'No check-in for 12 days'. Disk is fine at 54.7% free (140/256 GB), so low disk space (KB-017) is ruled out. I've asked her for symptoms, when it started and how often, recent updates or installs, and when she last restarted (KB-019 quick checks). I've also asked her to bring the laptop online so it can check in. The 12-day gap in check-ins may be the issue itself (won't boot or can't connect) or she may just not be using it. Once she replies, check for earlier tickets about the same problem. If it's slow or freezing, follow KB-019. If it's crashing, blue screens, or won't boot or connect, escalate.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-019",
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "low"
}
